# Agent Rule

## Information

If you are less than 80% confident before starting, search for information using the internet or MCP (context7), then respond.

## Response

After responding, cross-verify the provided information again using the internet or MCP (context7).

## Revision

Clearly verify and fix TypeScript issues, lint problems, and import issues. When making modifications, always search for the latest information using the internet or MCP (context7) first before proceeding.
Reference the package.json version information rather than using the latest versions.

## Code Writing

Always search for and follow the same patterns as existing components, storybooks, etc. when writing new code.
This guideline emphasizes maintaining consistency by referencing and following established patterns in the codebase, whether you're creating new components, writing storybooks, or implementing other types of code.
